    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Born into the shi class of Lu and raised in poverty, Confucius began teaching after he turned 30 and accepted students whatever their background.</li><li>As an official of Lu he tried to restore the duke's authority by having the three great families raze their walled strongholds, failed at the last of them and left the state in 497 BCE.</li><li>His teaching that government should rest on virtue and ritual rather than law and punishment became the official philosophy of imperial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu of Han</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Confucius asked no tuition of a prospective student, only a symbolic gift of a bundle of dried meat. The name Confucius itself was coined in the late 16th century by early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> missionaries to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, as a Latinized form of Kongfuzi.</p></aside>
    </section>

